# $DEV for CONF=term: what `rc ../port/mkdevlist term` prints
# (sys/src/9/port/mkdevlist: sed '/^$/d; /^#/d' term | awk ... -- for
# each line of the `dev` section, "dev" $1 ".z", then $3..$NF, each with
# ".z").  Derived BY HAND from that script and sys/src/9/hobbit/term,
# not generated: replace this file with the script's own output (one
# name per line, as here) once rc, sed and awk run on the model.  The
# blank line in term's dev section (between ip and bit) is deleted by the
# sed first, so bit and kprof belong to the section.
# Cross-check: the shipped kernel image hobbit/s9term carries 21 devices
# in the order of the device-character string "/ce|psMd2trikSwlaPIbT"
# (docs/s9term.md, on master) -- term's dev section in this order,
# root / ... kprof T, one per `dev` line below.
devroot.z
devcons.z
devenv.z
devpipe.z
devproc.z
devsrv.z
devmnt.z
devdup.z
deviic.z
deveia.z
devrtc.z
devincon.z
devdk.z
devscsi.z
scsi.z
scsibuf.z
devwren.z
devether.z
devarp.z
deviproute.z
devip.z
tcpinput.z
tcpoutput.z
tcptimer.z
tcpif.z
stil.z
devbit.z
bbmalloc.z
screen.z
kbd.z
devkprof.z
